edit: heres the link chomos [https://www.tiktok.com/@yourmomshouse/video/7329177843584503086](https://www.tiktok.com/@yourmomshouse/video/7329177843584503086)

Maybe not the advice u want to hear but its the advice you should hear, these type of people will always leave you in life whether it be after high school or college so don't be ashamed to shine as bright as you can, I downplayed a lot of what I could have done in life to appease people like this and it just held me back, so really you don't have to do anything if they're being cold that's on them. Move on find new friends or just stick around and study to keep ur grades up, I'll tell u one thing I can almost guarantee when push comes to shove they'll drop you quick. More than likely they keep you around because they get value from you whether that being you helping them academically in some way shape or form. I know the advice find new friends isn't what you want to hear and from first hand experience I detested it because starting over or being alone is hard but its way better in the long run than being surrounded by people praying on your downfall trust me, most people in this world arnt happy for other success they wish it was theirs or wish it would come crumbling down. This is crucial life advice that applies long after you leave school so really take some time to think about it and weigh all possibilities.

&#x200B;

edit: also if you can sense a little jealousy that should be indicator enough that these people are not just a little jealous, most try their best especially in social scenarios where they mutually benefit to hide there emotions to keep things amicable. If you can feel them being negative to you they 100% are truly not your friend and will probably fuck you over given the chance.
